ame=\"query\" id=\"search\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<button type=\"submit\" class=\"btn\">Search</button>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</form>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n\r\n</header>    <!--endnoindex-->\n    \n         \r\n    \r\n\r\n \r\n    \r\n\r\n<main id=\"main-content\" class=\"main container-fluid\">\r\n<section data-hero=\"scholarship\"><div><h1>European Undergraduate Scholarship - 2027-28</h1><p>The University of Bradford is pleased to offer the European Undergraduate Scholarship to students from eligible European Union countries commencing undergraduate study in the 2027/28 academic year.</p><p>The scholarship reflects the University's commitment to maintaining strong educational links with Europe and provides a reduced tuition fee rate for eligible students.</p><p>For 2027/28 entry, the scholarship has been designed so that eligible EU students pay a tuition fee equivalent to the maximum UK undergraduate fee plus 20%, resulting in a net annual fee of \u00a312,060.</p><p>The scholarship is awarded automatically and no separate application is required.</p></div><div data-device=\"top-left\"><dl data-type=\"table\"><dt><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon\" width=\"14\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" aria-hidden data-icon=\"clock\"><path d=\"M464 256A208 208 0 1 1 48 256a208 208 0 1 1 416 0zM0 256a256 256 0 1 0 512 0A256 256 0 1 0 0 256zM232 120V256c0 8 4 15.5 10.7 20l96 64c11 7.4 25.9 4.4 33.3-6.7s4.4-25.9-6.7-33.3L280 243.2V120c0-13.3-10.7-24-24-24s-24 10.7-24 24z\"/></svg>Attendance</dt><div data-field=\"attendance\"><dd data-value=\"full-time\">Full-time</dd></div><dt><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon\" width=\"14\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" aria-hidden data-icon=\"building-columns\"><path d=\"M243.4 2.6l-224 96c-14 6-21.8 21-18.7 35.8S16.8 160 32 160v8c0 13.3 10.7 24 24 24H456c13.3 0 24-10.7 24-24v-8c15.2 0 28.3-10.7 31.3-25.6s-4.8-29.9-18.7-35.8l-224-96c-8-3.4-17.2-3.4-25.2 0zM128 224H64V420.3c-.6 .3-1.2 .7-1.8 1.1l-48 32c-11.7 7.8-17 22.4-12.9 35.9S17.9 512 32 512H480c14.1 0 26.5-9.2 30.6-22.7s-1.1-28.1-12.9-35.9l-48-32c-.6-.4-1.2-.7-1.8-1.1V224H384V416H344V224H280V416H232V224H168V416H128V224zM256 64a32 32 0 1 1 0 64 32 32 0 1 1 0-64z\"/></svg>Available for</dt><div data-field=\"audience\"><dd data-value=\"prospective-students\">Prospective students</dd></div><dt><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon\" width=\"14\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" aria-hidden data-icon=\"calendar-days\"><path d=\"M152 24c0-13.3-10.7-24-24-24s-24 10.7-24 24V64H64C28.7 64 0 92.7 0 128v16 48V448c0 35.3 28.7 64 64 64H384c35.3 0 64-28.7 64-64V192 144 128c0-35.3-28.7-64-64-64H344V24c0-13.3-10.7-24-24-24s-24 10.7-24 24V64H152V24zM48 192h80v56H48V192zm0 104h80v64H48V296zm128 0h96v64H176V296zm144 0h80v64H320V296zm80-48H320V192h80v56zm0 160v40c0 8.8-7.2 16-16 16H320V408h80zm-128 0v56H176V408h96zm-144 0v56H64c-8.8 0-16-7.2-16-16V408h80zM272 248H176V192h96v56z\"/></svg>Entry year</dt><dd data-field=\"entry-year\">2027-28</dd><dt><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon\" width=\"14\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 512\" aria-hidden data-icon=\"graduation-cap\"><path d=\"M320 32c-8.1 0-16.1 1.4-23.7 4.1L15.8 137.4C6.3 140.9 0 149.9 0 160s6.3 19.1 15.8 22.6l57.9 20.9C57.3 229.3 48 259.8 48 291.9v28.1c0 28.4-10.8 57.7-22.3 80.8c-6.5 13-13.9 25.8-22.5 37.6C0 442.7-.9 448.3 .9 453.4s6 8.9 11.2 10.2l64 16c4.2 1.1 8.7 .3 12.4-2s6.3-6.1 7.1-10.4c8.6-42.8 4.3-81.2-2.1-108.7C90.3 344.3 86 329.8 80 316.5V291.9c0-30.2 10.2-58.7 27.9-81.5c12.9-15.5 29.6-28 49.2-35.7l157-61.7c8.2-3.2 17.5 .8 20.7 9s-.8 17.5-9 20.7l-157 61.7c-12.4 4.9-23.3 12.4-32.2 21.6l159.6 57.6c7.6 2.7 15.6 4.1 23.7 4.1s16.1-1.4 23.7-4.1L624.2 182.6c9.5-3.4 15.8-12.5 15.8-22.6s-6.3-19.1-15.8-22.6L343.7 36.1C336.1 33.4 328.1 32 320 32zM128 408c0 35.3 86 72 192 72s192-36.7 192-72L496.7 262.6 354.5 314c-11.1 4-22.8 6-34.5 6s-23.5-2-34.5-6L143.3 262.6 128 408z\"/></svg>Study level</dt><div data-field=\"study-level\"><dd data-value=\"x\">Undergraduate</dd></div><dt><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon\" width=\"14\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" aria-hidden data-icon=\"user-graduate\"><path d=\"M219.3 .5c3.1-.6 6.3-.6 9.4 0l200 40C439.9 42.7 448 52.6 448 64s-8.1 21.3-19.3 23.5L352 102.9V160c0 70.7-57.3 128-128 128s-128-57.3-128-128V102.9L48 93.3v65.1l15.7 78.4c.9 4.7-.3 9.6-3.3 13.3s-7.6 5.9-12.4 5.9H16c-4.8 0-9.3-2.1-12.4-5.9s-4.3-8.6-3.3-13.3L16 158.4V86.6C6.5 83.3 0 74.3 0 64C0 52.6 8.1 42.7 19.3 40.5l200-40zM111.9 327.7c10.5-3.4 21.8 .4 29.4 8.5l71 75.5c6.3 6.7 17 6.7 23.3 0l71-75.5c7.6-8.1 18.9-11.9 29.4-8.5C401 348.6 448 409.4 448 481.3c0 17-13.8 30.7-30.7 30.7H30.7C13.8 512 0 498.2 0 481.3c0-71.9 47-132.7 111.9-153.6z\"/></svg>Available scholarships</dt><dd data-field=\"availability\">Unlimited</dd></dl><a href=\"#apply\" class=\"btn\">How to apply</a></div></section><section><h2 id=\"overview\">Overview</h2><p>The University of Bradford is pleased to offer the European Undergraduate Scholarship to students from eligible European Union countries commencing undergraduate study in the 2027/28 academic year.</p><p>The scholarship reflects the University's commitment to maintaining strong educational links with Europe and provides a reduced tuition fee rate for eligible students.</p><p>For 2027/28 entry, the scholarship has been designed so that eligible EU students pay a tuition fee equivalent to the maximum UK undergraduate fee plus 20%, resulting in a net annual fee of \u00a312,060.</p><p>The scholarship is awarded automatically and no separate application is required.</p><h3 id=\"payment\">Payment amount and frequency</h3><p><strong>Payment Amount and Frequency</strong></p><p>The scholarship is applied as a tuition fee reduction each year of study, subject to eligibility and continued enrolment.</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Course Type</strong></td><td><strong>Standard International Fee</strong></td><td><strong>Scholarship Value</strong></td><td><strong>Net Annual Fee Payable</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Classroom-based Programmes</td><td>\u00a316,500</td><td>\u00a34,440</td><td>\u00a312,060</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory-based Programmes</td><td>\u00a317,312</td><td>\u00a35,252</td><td>\u00a312,060</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>The scholarship will normally be applied for each year of study and will be reflected directly within the student's tuition fee assessment.</p></section><section><h2 id=\"eligibility\">Eligibility</h2><p>To be eligible for the European Undergraduate Scholarship, applicants must:</p><ul><li>Be classified as an international fee-paying student.</li><li>Be ordinarily resident in an eligible European Union member state.</li><li>Hold an offer for a full-time undergraduate programme at the University of Bradford.</li><li>Be enrolling in the 2027/28 academic year.</li><li>Meet all academic and admissions requirements for their chosen programme.</li><li>Be a new undergraduate entrant for 2027/28</li></ul><uob-disclosure><h3 id=\"applicable-courses\">Applicable courses</h3><p>All full time undegraduate courses</p></uob-disclosure><uob-disclosure><h3 id=\"eligible-countries\">Eligible countries</h3><ol><li>Afghanistan</li><li>Aland Islands</li><li>Albania</li><li>Algeria</li><li>American Samoa</li><li>Andorra</li><li>Angola</li><li>Anguilla</li><li>Antigua & Barbuda</li><li>Antilles (Netherlands)</li><li>Argentina</li><li>Armenia</li><li>Aruba</li><li>Australia</li><li>Austria</li><li>Azerbaijan</li><li>The Bahamas</li><li>Bahrain</li><li>Bangladesh</li><li>Barbados</li><li>Belarus</li><li>Belgium</li><li>Belize</li><li>Benin</li><li>Bermuda</li><li>Bhutan</li><li>Bolivia</li><li>Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba</li><li>Bosnia And Herzegovina</li><li>Botswana</li><li>Bouvet Island</li><li>Brazil</li><li>British Antarctic Territories</li><li>British Indian Ocean Territory</li><li>British Virgin Islands</li><li>Brunei Darussalam</li><li>Burkina Faso / Upper Volta</li><li>Bulgaria</li><li>Burundi</li><li>Myanmar</li><li>Cameroon</li><li>Canada</li><li>Cape Verde Islands</li><li>Cayman Islands</li><li>Canary Islands</li><li>Central African Republic</li><li>Chad</li><li>Channel Islands</li><li>Chile</li><li>China</li><li>Christmas Island</li><li>Cocos (Keeling) Islands</li><li>Colombia</li><li>Comoros</li><li>Congo (Peoples Republic)</li><li>Congo, Democratic Republic</li><li>Cook Islands</li><li>Costa Rica</li><li>Croatia</li><li>Cuba</li><li>Cura</li><li>Cyprus (European Union)</li><li>Cyprus (Non-European Union)</li><li>Czech Republic</li><li>Denmark</li><li>Djibouti</li><li>Dominica</li><li>Dominican Republic</li><li>Timor Leste (East Timor)</li><li>Ecuador</li><li>United Arab Republic of Egypt</li><li>El Salvador</li><li>England</li><li>Equatorial Guinea</li><li>Eritrea</li><li>Estonia</li><li>Ethiopia</li><li>Falkland Islands (Malvinas)</li><li>Faroe Islands</li><li>Fiji</li><li>Finland</li><li>France</li><li>French Guiana</li><li>French Polynesia</li><li>Gabon</li><li>The Republic of The Gambia</li><li>Georgia</li><li>Germany</li><li>Ghana</li><li>Gibraltar</li><li>Greece</li><li>Greenland</li><li>Grenada</li><li>Guadeloupe</li><li>Guam</li><li>Guatemala</li><li>Guernsey</li><li>Guinea</li><li>Guinea Bissau</li><li>Guyana</li><li>Haiti</li><li>Honduras</li><li>Hong Kong</li><li>Hungary</li><li>Iceland</li><li>India</li><li>Indonesia</li><li>Iran</li><li>Iraq</li><li>The Republic of Ireland</li><li>Isle of Man</li><li>Israel</li><li>Italy</li><li>Cote D'Ivoire (Ivory Coast)</li><li>Jamaica</li><li>Japan</li><li>Jersey</li><li>Jordan</li><li>Cambodia</li><li>Kazakhstan</li><li>Kenya</li><li>Kiribati (The Gilbert Islands)</li><li>Democratic People's Republic of Korea (North)</li><li>Republic of Korea (South)</li><li>Kosovo</li><li>Kuwait</li><li>Kyrgyzstan</li><li>Laos People's Democratic Republic</li><li>Latvia</li><li>Lebanon</li><li>Lesotho</li><li>Li